<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Strict warnings are introduced in stages, not all at once.

    The pre-migration code has ~30 `async` methods with no `await` (CS1998) and widespread
    nullable-reference violations. Promoting those to errors here would make Phase 0 unable to
    reach a green build, which defeats the purpose of Phase 0 as a checkpoint that isolates
    "the framework upgrade broke it" from "the rewrite broke it".

    Phase 3 turns the following on once the offending code has been rewritten:
      <WarningsAsErrors>CS1998;CS4014;CS8600;CS8602;CS8618;RMG012;RMG020</WarningsAsErrors>
    RMG012/RMG020 are Mapperly's unmapped-member diagnostics — promoting them is what makes
    Mapperly a real safety upgrade over AutoMapper rather than just a licensing change.
  -->

</Project>
